# Allowlist for bin/design-tokens.
#
# Format: <path> | <one-line reason>
#   - A path ending in "/" is a directory prefix (every file under it).
#   - Any other path is an exact file match.
#
# Every entry needs a reason that still holds; an entry whose reason has
# expired (the file no longer does what it says) should be deleted, not kept
# "just in case".
#
# Prefer an exact file to a directory, because a directory entry also exempts
# every file added to it later, under a reason that may not apply to them.
# `lib/config/` was measured and rejected on exactly that ground: only
# `wind_theme.g.dart` is generated, and every other file in that directory is
# hand-authored, so the directory form would have exempted them all under a reason
# that is false for each one. Four of those hand-authored files are the token
# supplements (`depools_status_tokens.dart`, `_paper_tokens.dart`,
# `_overlay_tokens.dart`, `_control_tokens.dart`), and they DO carry hex values;
# they need no exemption: this tool measures `Color(0x...)` and `Colors.*` Dart
# literals, and a hex inside a Wind alias string is outside that pattern by design.
# What guards those four files instead is `bin/verify-design-contrast.py`, which
# parses them and checks every pair it finds.
#
# One entry is the whole list, and keeping it that way is the point: an entry is a
# hole in the token rule, so it is added only when there is a reason that will
# still hold in six months.

lib/config/wind_theme.g.dart | generated by design:sync from DESIGN.md; not hand-authored
